        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "## Question 1 \n",
        "To estimate the average weight of all Chihuahuas, we took a random sample with replacement of 1,000 Chihuahuas from around the world, weighed them, and calculated the average weight to be 3.9 pounds. We report a 95\\% confidence interval of [3.6, 4.2]. Which of the following is true? Select all that apply.  \n",
        "\\begin{itemize}\n",
        "\\item (a) There is a 95\\% chance that the average weight of all Chihuahuas in the world is between 3.6 and 4.2 pounds. \\\\\n",
        "\\item (b) If we repeated this procedure many times, 95\\% of the intervals calculated this way will include the mean weight of all Chihuahuas in the world.\\\\\n",
        "\\item (c) The interval [3.6,4.2] corresponds to the middle 95\\% of the bootstrap estimated sampling distribution. \\\\\n",
        "\\item (d) There is a 95\\% chance the average weight of all Chihuahuas in the world is 3.9 pounds. \n",
        "\\end{itemize}\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "```{tex}\n",
        "%A D-20 is a 20-sided die with the whole numbers 1 to 20 on each face, each of which is equally likely to be rolled. \n",
        "\n",
        "%\\begin{enumerate}\n",
        "%\\item Write out the probability mass function of this experiment. \n",
        "\n",
        "%\\vspace{3cm}\n",
        "\n",
        "%\\item What is the expectation of a roll? \n",
        "\n",
        "%\\end{enumerate}\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Question 2\n",
        "Below is a proof using properties/rules of expectations. Select the correct rule being used at each point. \n",
        "\n",
        "For a sample $Y$ randomly drawn from a population with mean $\\mu$, the sample mean is an unbiased estimator for the population mean: $E[\\bar{Y}] = \\mu$ \n",
        "\n",
        "\\begin{tabular}{l l }\n",
        "\n",
        "$\\bar{Y} = \\frac{1}{n} \\sum_{i=1}^N Y_i$ & definition of sample mean\\\\\n",
        "& \\\\\n",
        "$E[\\bar{Y}] = E[\\frac{1}{n} \\sum_{i=1}^N Y_i]$ & take expectation of estimator\\\\\n",
        "& \\\\\n",
        "$ \\frac{1}{n} E[ \\sum_{i=1}^N Y_i]$ &  (a) Constant Rule \\\\\n",
        " & (b) Linearity of Expectations \\\\\n",
        " & (c) Irrelevant Conditioning \\\\\n",
        " & (d) Law of Iterated Expectations \\\\\n",
        "$ \\frac{1}{n} E[ Y_1 + Y_2 + Y_3 + ... + Y_n]$ & \\\\\n",
        "& \\\\\n",
        "$ \\frac{1}{n}( E[ Y_1] + E[Y_2] + E[Y_3] + ... + E[Y_n])$ &  (a) Constant Rule \\\\\n",
        " & (b) Linearity of Expectations \\\\\n",
        " & (c) Irrelevant Conditioning \\\\\n",
        " & (d) Law of Iterated Expectations \\\\\n",
        " & \\\\\n",
        "$\\frac{1}{n}( E[ Y] + E[Y] + E[Y] + ... + E[Y])$ (n times) & Y's are IID\\\\\n",
        "& \\\\\n",
        "$ \\frac{1}{n}(\\mu + \\mu + \\mu + ... + \\mu)$ (n times) & by definition \\\\\n",
        "& \\\\\n",
        "$\\frac{1}{n} \\sum_{i=1}^n \\mu$ & \\\\ \n",
        "& \\\\\n",
        "$\\frac{1}{n} n\\mu$ & \\\\ \n",
        "& \\\\\n",
        "$=\\mu$ & \\\\\n",
        "\n",
        "\\end{tabular}"
      ],
